# Soma's plan, in John Carmack's .plan format: one item per line, under the
# day it was written. An unmarked line is open; a bid marks its item "+ "
# when done (or "* " the day it was written), "- " if dropped. Marked lines
# are pruned once they've landed, so the file holds what's left: `git log -p
# .plan` has the rest. The order is the priority. An item is a pointer: its
# details are in the files it names. Pantheon's docs/PLAN.md explains how its
# market drafts tasks from this file.
